{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"diagnosis\":\"The `ChoiceBisim.bisim` case exposes only its bisimilarity proof as a case field; the related processes are already represented by `s1` and `s2`. Therefore `case bisim p q h` supplies too many variable names. Match it as `case bisim h` and use `h.follow_fst`/`h.follow_snd`.\",\"proof_body\":\"by\\n  intro h\\n  exists @ChoiceBisim _ _ defs\\n  constructor\\n  · exact ChoiceBisim.choice h\\n  intro s1 s2 hr μ\\n  cases hr\\n  case choice p q r h =>\\n    constructor\\n    · intro s' htr\\n      cases htr\\n      case choiceL hp =>\\n        obtain ⟨q', hq, hpq⟩ := h.follow_fst hp\\n        exact ⟨q', Tr.choiceL hq, ChoiceBisim.bisim hpq⟩\\n      case choiceR hr =>\\n        exact ⟨_, Tr.choiceR hr,\\n          ChoiceBisim.bisim (HomBisimilarity.refl _)⟩\\n    · intro s' htr\\n      cases htr\\n      case choiceL hq =>\\n        obtain ⟨p', hp, hpq⟩ := h.follow_snd hq\\n        exact ⟨p', Tr.choiceL hp, ChoiceBisim.bisim hpq⟩\\n      case choiceR hr =>\\n        exact ⟨_, Tr.choiceR hr,\\n          ChoiceBisim.bisim (HomBisimilarity.refl _)⟩\\n  case bisim h =>\\n    constructor\\n    · intro p' hp\\n      obtain ⟨q', hq, hpq⟩ := h.follow_fst hp\\n      exact ⟨q', hq, ChoiceBisim.bisim hpq⟩\\n    · intro q' hq\\n      obtain ⟨p', hp, hpq⟩ := h.follow_snd hq\\n      exact ⟨p', hp, ChoiceBisim.bisim hpq⟩\"}"}}
